	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(20.0, 20.0, 620.0, 96.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">PRAKTIKUM 7 — Classification

THE POINT OF THIS WORKFLOW: every learner meets Test and Score on the SAME
folds with the SAME preprocessing. That is what makes the comparison fair.
Constant is the do-nothing baseline -- if a model cannot beat it, it has learned nothing.</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(890.0, 260.0, 340.0, 270.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">WHAT TO DO
1. Test and Score: 'Cross validation, 5 folds'.
   Sort by AUC. Does every model beat Constant?
2. Set Target class = 'yes' (the minority class).
   Watch precision and recall change completely.
3. Confusion Matrix: select the FALSE NEGATIVE cell
   and look at those rows in the Data Table.
   What do the missed defaulters have in common?
4. Tree Viewer: set depth to 3. Can you read the
   rules aloud? That is why trees survive in
   regulated domains.
5. Calibration Plot: compare Naive Bayes with
   Logistic Regression. NB hugs the extremes --
   its probabilities are not trustworthy.

UTS PREP: be able to explain every number here.</text>
	</annotations>
